 2026-10-19 speakzzz
  * Version 3.1.11
  * Security: !timer start is BOSS OWNER only. A timer runs its text as a
    Tcl command (the same as !tcl), so an OWNER could run anything and
    make himself BOSS or reach the shell. !timer list and kill unchanged
  * langcheck.tcl also reads the scripts and lists messages the code asks
    for that English doesn't have (the command stops there in every
    language). Fixed what it found:
    - !man lang stopped after its first line and never listed the
      languages (man.487_2, now man.487_1, which also lists FR now)
    - !man ho never showed the mass halfop line (man.884_5, now man.884_1)
    - !ho - did nothing while X was on the channel (it tried to send a
      message that never existed); it now skips X and carries on
    - !set defaultlang with an unknown language stopped with an error;
      it now says which languages are available (egg.5)
    - removed code that could never run: a CTCP VERSION reply handler,
      two !show entries for the old GuestNick feature, and a second
      backchan check that the first one already covers
 2026-10-18 speakzzz
  * Version 3.1.10
  * New tools/langcheck.tcl: a translation checker run from the shell
    (tclsh BlackTools/tools/langcheck.tcl). It compares every language
    file with English and lists missing messages, misspelled names,
    messages set twice, and %placeholders% a translation leaves out.
  * Fixed everything it found:
    - FR: !seen and !info failed (seen.27-41 and info.20 were missing),
      the SILENCE messages were filed under the wrong name, an untranslated
      English copy of the Private messages removed, vote list shows Expires
    - ES: added autoupdate.49 and gl.noxonly; fixed broken placeholders
      ("% msg.1%", "% chan%", "char%") that showed up literally, the
      voiceme text that was split over several lines, unfinished unban
      replies, ban replies now show the ban ID, stray "005" text removed
    - RO: badquitpart.10 had the wrong name, manual for
      badchan-floodcontrol added, small manual gaps filled
    - All: autobroadcast.6 showed no number (it used %msg.2%), seen.41
      showed a literal %num%, private.11 printed "none", ub.4 had a
      colour code instead of bold, man.1181 showed "%set%set"
 2026-10-18 speakzzz
  * Version 3.1.9
  * A refused ban now says why instead of doing nothing silently: the
    mask would match the bot itself (b.15), or a protected user, who
    is named (b.16). New lang strings in EN, RO, FR, ES
 2026-10-18 speakzzz
  * Version 3.1.8
  * addhost and myset addhost refuse host masks that would match lots of
    people, such as *!*@*, *!*@*.net or nick!*@*. Everyone matching a
    user's mask is recognized as that user and gets their access, so a
    single typo could give every visitor owner or master access.
    A mask is refused when its ident part is only wildcards and its host
    part has fewer than two labels without wildcards; normal masks like
    *!*@*.example.net, *!*@1.2.3.* and *!ident@* still work
  * New lang string addhost.3 (EN, RO, FR, ES)
 2026-10-18 speakzzz
  * Version 3.1.7
  * link by private message now needs owner or master, as in the
    channel and the other command forms; a global op could link
    channels by private message
  * clonescan by private message now works for channel ops, as it
    does in the channel
 2026-10-18 speakzzz
  * Version 3.1.6
  * inviteban: the inviter's host comes from the INVITE itself instead
    of a USERHOST request. The next USERHOST reply used to be taken as
    the answer, so a reply meant for another feature (secure mode, !ub,
    !sb, ...) could get an unrelated user banned. In an invite flood
    only the first inviter was handled, with the last invite's channel
    in the reason. Also removed the stray ":" in the reason
  * clonescan: the bot itself and exempt users are no longer counted
    (a shell running several bots got its own host banned), and users
    of a web chat gateway (webchat_hosts) are grouped by ident, so one
    gateway's users aren't all banned as clones of each other
  * antijoinflood: the channel lock sets "+mr" instead of "+m r", which
    only set +m; the unlock removes both modes again
 2026-10-18 speakzzz
  * Version 3.1.5
  * noproxy: the proxy lookup now runs in the background. It used to
    make two blocking requests to ip-api.com per join, freezing the
    whole bot for up to 13 seconds each time (no kicks, bans or replies,
    and a join flood could freeze it for minutes), and gave a Tcl error
    on every join while ip-api.com was unreachable
  * noproxy: one lookup per host, results remembered for
    noproxy:cachetime minutes (default 360), at most noproxy:rate
    lookups a minute (default 40; the free service allows 45). Users
    who joined while a lookup was pending are handled when it returns,
    if they are still on the channel. Lookup problems are logged at
    most once every 10 minutes
 2026-10-18 speakzzz
  * Version 3.1.4
  * AntiTake (dontdeop / dontop): "is this the bot?" is now an exact
    nick comparison (isbotnick). Nicks like [s]aga, sag[a] or sag\a
    were treated as the bot, so their deops and ops were never reverted
  * Timer lookups built from a nick, host, channel or handle now escape
    [ ] * ? and \ (new blacktools:glob_escape). For users or channels
    with brackets, the old timer wasn't found, so it kept running and
    could reset flood counters early (channel flood, join flood, nick
    flood, BadChan, badnick, VoiceOnMsg, Seen, command flood, and more)
 2026-10-18 speakzzz
  * Version 3.1.3
  * Word lists (antipub, antibadword, antispam, badquitpart, badrealname,
    badnick, badident, badhost): each pattern is now matched against
    every word as well as the whole text, so "*.com" catches
    "join spam.com now", not only messages ending in ".com". Trailing
    punctuation is ignored ("spam.com,")
  * Exceptions in BlackTools.tcl (antipubexcept, except_badwords, etc.)
    now work with wildcards: "*youtube.com*" really allows YouTube links,
    which used to get people banned
  * antibadword: a bad word's own action method (e.g. "*pula*:3") no
    longer carries over to the bad words listed after it; with the
    default list every bad word got an immediate ban (method 3) instead
    of kick -> ban (method 6)
  * BadChan: the default bad channel list in BlackTools.tcl
    (badcchannels) never matched anything; it now works
 2026-10-18 speakzzz
  * Version 3.1.2
  * anticaps: capitals are counted as a share of the letters instead of
    the whole message, so spacing letters out ("H E L L O") or padding
    with punctuation ("HELLO!!!!!!") no longer dilutes shouting below
    the limit. Emoticons (":D", ":-P", "XD") and nicks of people on the
    channel are left out; messages need 20+ characters and 10+ letters
  * antirepeat: messages are compared ignoring capitalization,
    formatting codes and extra spaces, so "buy now", "BUY NOW" and
    "buy  now" count as the same message. Fixed a repeated message
    containing * or ? cancelling the timers of other messages
  * anticolor also catches hex colors and reverse text. When
    anticolor:specific_colors is set, a hit now stops the protections
    after it, as all other hits do, instead of letting them punish the
    same message again
 2026-10-18 speakzzz
  * Version 3.1.1
  * repetitivechars now checks every run of identical characters in a
    message, not only the last one: "nooooooooo really" or
    "!!!!!!!!!! spam" used to get through. Whitespace ends a run and
    never counts, so indented or aligned text can't trigger it
  * repetitivechars: a per-channel limit that isn't a number of at
    least 2 now falls back to the default; before, a limit of 1 made
    every message count as a violation
 2026-10-18 speakzzz
  * Version 3.1.0: brings in the working changes from the original
    author's BlackTools 3.0 branch (2024-2025):
    - Idle: new +b option (idleban) bans regular users who idle longer
      than idlebanmax; settings idlebanmax, idleban:banmask and
      idleban:bantime in BlackTools.tcl
    - Alias: one alias can run several commands separated by |
    - New channel flag disablepubcmds turns off public (!) commands
    - Seen: no longer reveals that someone was seen in a private or
      secret channel
    - Notes: read, delete and delete-all no longer depend on the
      capitalization of the handle
  * Not taken from 3.0 because they are broken there: the rewritten
    repetitivechars and antichanflood protections (they error on every
    message and stop the protections after them), the BT.Timers.tcl
    duplication, and the curl/tar updater
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Version 2.6.0: first release of this fork
    (https://github.com/speakzzz/BlackTools-TCL). Includes all fork
    changes listed below since the original 2.5.5
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Boss owners are warned by note when the bot can't save its data
    (user file folder, channel file folder or BlackTools FILES folder
    missing, not writable or full), and told again once it's fixed.
    Checked a minute after loading and every hour, using a real test
    write. New lang strings loader.3 and loader.4 (EN, RO, FR, ES)
  * Load/storage problems are only marked as reported once an owner
    was reached; otherwise they are retried every 5 minutes. Before,
    a bot started with -m (no owners yet) never sent the note
  * If a note can't be stored, owners who are online get a notice
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Boss owners now get a note when module, command or protection
    files fail to load and are skipped, and another once everything
    loads fine again. Notes are sent a minute after loading, only when
    the set of problems changes, in each owner's language, and not to
    owners with notes turned off
  * New lang strings loader.1 and loader.2 (EN, RO, FR, ES)
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Fixed BT.TCL.tcl failing to load (logged "can't read tmp" on every
    load): two leftover lines from the atomic-write change ran at load
    time. The .tcl commands were unaffected
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Settings changed from IRC (nick, realname, homechan, cmdchar, etc.)
    are now escaped correctly when written to eggdrop.conf or
    BlackTools.tcl. Values containing " \ $ [ or ] could previously
    leave the config unloadable, be saved wrongly, or run code when the
    config was loaded. One shared helper (config:quote) replaces the
    partial per-setting escaping
  * away: messages containing quotes are no longer sent with \"
  * nick: nicknames containing { } are no longer altered or rejected
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * New blacktools:write_atomic: files are written to a temp file and
    renamed into place, so a crash or full disk can never leave them
    half-written or missing. Original permissions are kept
  * AutoUpdate now writes eggdrop.conf (twice during an update) and
    BlackTools.tcl this way instead of overwriting them in place
  * Editing eggdrop.conf from IRC (config:save) no longer deletes the
    file before replacing it, and keeps its permissions
  * .tcl load/unload use the shared helper
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Braced all 515 expr calls outside Addons/ (e.g. expr $a + 1 ->
    expr {$a + 1}) and turned 86 simple counters into incr. Braced
    expressions are compiled once instead of re-parsed on every call,
    and values from IRC or data files can no longer be evaluated as
    code inside an expression. No intended behavior change: each
    conversion was checked by running old and new forms side by side
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * Loader: a module, command or protection file that fails to load is
    now logged (with line number) and skipped instead of killing the
    bot; a summary of problems is logged after loading. Core files
    (Core, Binds, Ban, Timers, language) are still required
  * Loader: fixed module names being misread when loading from the
    update backup folder (scripts/BT.backup), which broke the special
    handling of a failed AutoUpdate module during updates
  * Loader: files now load in a fixed (sorted) order on every system
 2026-09-28 speakzzz
  * .tcl wget: HTTPS-only downloads via Tcl's http package (wget no longer
    needed), async so the bot does not block, 1 MB size limit, up to 3
    https redirects, rejects web pages and incomplete Tcl scripts, writes
    via temp file so partial downloads never appear in scripts/
  * .tcl wget/load/unload/info: script names are validated (no paths,
    no "..", must end in .tcl); load refuses missing files and BlackTools
  * .tcl wget: download errors go to the requester by notice instead of
    raw wget output in the channel; fixed wrong name in "already
    downloaded" message
  * eggdrop.conf is now written atomically and keeps its permissions
